   "reasoning": "We need answer user's request: produce complete solution as ONE fenced Python code block. Need define ADJUSTERS and adjust. Need preserve quirks. Need think carefully.\n\nWe need craft final code only. Need ensure no tests, no main.\n\nLet's analyze requirements deeply to avoid subtle behavior.\n\nLegacy:\ndef legacy_adjust(readings):\n    out = []\n    total = 0.0\n    for i, r in enumerate(readings):\n        kind = r.get('kind')\n        if kind == 'raw':\n            v = float(r['value'])\n            if v < 0:\n                v = 0.0\n            total = total + v\n            out = out + [{'i': i, 'kind': 'raw', 'value': round(v, 3), 'total': round(total, 3)}]\n        elif kind == 'scaled':\n            v = float(r['value']) * float(r.get('gain', 1.0))\n            v = round(v, 2)\n            total = total + v\n            out = out + [{'i': i, 'kind': 'scaled', 'value': v, 'total': round(total, 3)}]\n        elif kind == 'offset':\n            v = float(r['value']) + float(r.get('bias', 0.0))\n            if v < 0:\n                v = 0.0\n            r['value'] = v\n            total = total + v\n            out = out + [{'i': i, 'kind': 'offset', 'value': round(v, 3), 'total': round(total, 3)}]\n        elif kind == 'skip':\n            out = out + [{'i': i, 'kind': 'skip', 'value': 0.0, 'total': round(total, 3)}]\n        else:\n            raise ValueError('unknown kind: %r' % (kind,))\n    return out\n\nNeed ADJUSTERS dict keys exactly four strings. Values callables handler(state, index, record) -> dict. state dict holding running total under 'total' float. Handler does branch arithmetic, side effects, updates state['total'] exactly as legacy, returns row. Must work direct with caller-supplied state non-zero.\n\nadjust(readings):\n- fresh state = {'total': 0.0} every call\n- walk input with enumerate, reading kind as record.get('kind')\n- for each record, look handler up in module-level ADJUSTERS at call time and call exactly once. R